# Build directories
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user
*.sln.docstates
CMakeSettings.json

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Testing/

# Compiled objects / binaries
*.obj
*.o
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Third-party fetched sources (vendor via CMake FetchContent / submodules, not committed)
third_party/*
!third_party/.gitkeep

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Large data / meshes / results (track via Git LFS or external storage instead)
*.msh
*.vtu
*.vtk
/data/
/results/

# ...except the small fixtures the test suite actually reads. These are not
# "large data": together they are well under 150 KB, and excluding them means
# a fresh clone fails tests/test_gmsh_reader.cpp rather than merely lacking a
# convenience.
#
# The validation_box pair especially must be tracked: they were written by
# Gmsh itself and are the only fixtures in this project it did not author, so
# they cannot be regenerated without Gmsh installed -- which is exactly the
# situation this reader was written in. See tools/gmsh_validation_box.geo.
#
# coax_via.msh (~1.2 MB) is tracked too, despite being regenerable from
# tools/coax_via.geo. It is the Phase 01 Sec. 7.1 target problem -- the mesh
# Phase 04 assembles on and Phase 05 must reproduce Z_0, L', C' and R_DC
# from -- so having it present means that work starts against the exact
# geometry these results were measured on, rather than one regenerated by a
# different Gmsh version with different entity numbering or mesh sizing.
# Reproducibility of the benchmark is worth more here than the file size.
!meshes/cube_2.msh
!meshes/cube_4.msh
!meshes/cube_6.msh
!meshes/validation_box_v22.msh
!meshes/validation_box_v41.msh
!meshes/coax_via.msh
